1. Create the Directory Structure
Inside your workspace directory, create a subfolder called modules/aws-s3-bucket:

Plaintext
devops-docs/
├── main.tf                     <-- Root Configuration
└── modules/
    └── aws-s3-bucket/          <-- Local Child Module Folder
        ├── main.tf
        ├── variables.tf
        └── outputs.tf

2. Write the Child Module Code
modules/aws-s3-bucket/variables.tf
Define input variables that your root module will pass into this custom module:

Terraform
variable "bucket_name" {
  type        = string
  description = "The name of the S3 bucket"
}

variable "environment" {
  type        = string
  description = "Deployment environment (dev, stage, prod)"
  default     = "dev"
}

modules/aws-s3-bucket/main.tf
Define the AWS resources inside the module:

Terraform
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "this" {
  bucket = var.bucket_name

  tags = {
    Name        = var.bucket_name
    Environment = var.environment
    ManagedBy   = "Terraform"
  }
}
modules/aws-s3-bucket/outputs.tf
Expose values back to the root module:

Terraform
output "bucket_arn" {
  value       = aws_s3_bucket.this.arn
  description = "ARN of the created S3 bucket"
}

 3. Call the Local Module from Root main.tfNow, edit the main.tf in your root folder to point directly to ./modules/aws-s3-bucket:Terraformterraform {
  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source  = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = "~> 5.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "aws" {
  region                      = "us-east-1"
  skip_credentials_validation = true
  skip_requesting_account_id  = true
}

# Call your local custom module using a relative path
module "my_practice_bucket" {
  source      = "./modules/aws-s3-bucket"
  bucket_name = "my-practice-app-bucket-2026"
  environment = "practice"
}
